The microphone sample rate reached the DSP as zero

q6cvp_send_media_format filled in media_format_info and ended up calling
q6dsp_map_channels() with the fields of channel_info. Both are members of the
SAME union (vss_icommon_param_data), so they share memory:

    media_format_info:  port_id@0  num_channels@4  bits_per_sample@6
                        sample_rate@8  channel_mapping@12
    channel_info:       num_channels@0  bits_per_sample@4  channel_mapping@8

Out of that came two pieces of damage on the last line of the function:

  - As the channel count it was passed channel_info.num_channels, which at
    offset 0 is really media_format_info.port_id: 0xb037, that is, 45111
    channels. q6dsp_map_channels returns -EINVAL with that and writes no map
    at all.

  - As the destination it was passed channel_info.channel_mapping, offset 8,
    which is where sample_rate had just been stored. And the first thing
    q6dsp_map_channels does is memset(ch_map, 0, PCM_MAX_NUM_CHANNEL), so it
    wiped out the 48000 that had just been put there.

Result: the transmit endpoint was declared to the DSP with sample rate 0 and a
blank channel map. The session is created without a single error --every CVP
command answers ok-- and the microphone's voice never reaches the modem. It is
exactly the symptom we had: the other end is heard but we are not heard.

Reception survived because the DSP already knows the output port configuration
from the AFE and does not depend on this parameter to play back.

Found on 2026-08-10, after checking with the voice session traced that the
microphone port did reach RUNNING throughout the whole call.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
 	cmd.param_data.media_format_info.bits_per_sample = 16;
 	cmd.param_data.media_format_info.sample_rate = 48000;

-	q6dsp_map_channels(cmd.param_data.channel_info.channel_mapping,
-			   cmd.param_data.channel_info.num_channels);
+	q6dsp_map_channels(cmd.param_data.media_format_info.channel_mapping,
+			   cmd.param_data.media_format_info.num_channels);

 	return q6voice_common_send(cvp, &cmd.hdr);
 }
